        "content": [
          "Core taught -ANTA, -INTA, -ONTA. Their",
          "time is RELATIVE to the main verb:",
          "A = same time, I = before, O = after.",
          "",
          "AS ADJECTIVES (-A):                   Press 1",
          "marŝanta orkestro  = a marching band",
          "la pasinta jaro    = last year",
          "la venonta kunveno = the next meeting",
          "",
          "AS PEOPLE (-O):                       Press 2",
          "la parolanto = the one speaking",
          "la gajninto  = the winner (who has won)",
          "la parolonto = the next speaker",
          "",
          "TIME IS RELATIVE:                     Press 3",
          "Mi vidis marŝantan orkestron.",
          "= I saw a band that was marching."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Marŝanta orkestro. La pasinta jaro. La venonta kunveno.",
          "2": "La parolanto. La gajninto. La parolonto.",
          "3": "Mi vidis marŝantan orkestron."
        },
        "pronunciation": "Leciono kvardek du"
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "WITH -E, a participle tells what the",
          "SUBJECT of the sentence does at the same",
          "time (-ante), before (-inte) or after (-onte):",
          "",
